## Original Content
<p>Today I’m excited to share that we are expanding our university content catalog with new certificates and Specializations that are designed to help learners develop the human and technical skills that matter most in an AI-powered future. Findings from more than 92,000 employers included in the QS World Future Skills Index 2027 show persistent gaps [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://blog.coursera.org/new-university-programs-help-learners-build-skills-for-the-ai-era/">New university programs help learners build human and technical skills for the AI era</a> appeared first on <a href="https://blog.coursera.org">Coursera Blog</a>.</p>

## Summary
Coursera is expanding its university content catalog with new certificates and Specializations to help learners develop human and technical skills for an AI-powered future. The programs are informed by insights from the QS World Future Skills Index 2027, which reveals skill gaps based on data from over 92,000 employers.

## Key Points
- Coursera introduces new educational programs focused on skills relevant to the AI era.
- The programs aim to enhance both human and technical competencies for learners.
- Insights are derived from the QS World Future Skills Index 2027, based on extensive employer data.
- The initiative addresses persistent skill gaps identified in the workforce by employers.


